{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"bee25b223e1cff35","name":"card_unit_cedar_division","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Japan/BloodIron/units/card_unit_cedar_division","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"CEDAR DIVISION","text":"Becomes Veteran if you have 4 or less kredit slots.","flavorText":"The 8th Infantry Division of the Imperial Japanese Army, formed in 1898, was nicknamed Cedar Division (杉兵団, Sugi-heidan). During WWII it served as part of the Kwantung Army in Manchuria until it was transferred to the Philippines in 1944. There, it took part in the intense combat against the US invasion. The 5th Infantry Regiment of 8th Division was transferred to Leyte in late July 1944, and by late December 1944 was nearly completely annihilated during the course of the Battle of Leyte. The remainder of the division were assigned to the 41st Army and suffered heavy losses during the Battle of Manila in January 1945. It fought on until the official surrender of Japan. It is partly famous for one of its officers, Hiroo Onada, a second lieutenant of the Division, who did not surrender until 10 March 1974.","faction":"Japan","type":"infantry","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":6,"operationCost":0,"attack":4,"defense":4},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_cedar_division","title":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_cedar_division_title","SourceString":"CEDAR DIVISION","LocalizedString":"CEDAR DIVISION"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":4,"defense":4,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Japan","kredits":6,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_cedar_division_text","SourceString":"Becomes Veteran if you have 4 or less kredit slots.","LocalizedString":"Becomes Veteran if you have 4 or less kredit slots."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_cedar_division_history","SourceString":"The 8th Infantry Division of the Imperial Japanese Army, formed in 1898, was nicknamed Cedar Division (杉兵団, Sugi-heidan). During WWII it served as part of the Kwantung Army in Manchuria until it was transferred to the Philippines in 1944. There, it took part in the intense combat against the US invasion. The 5th Infantry Regiment of 8th Division was transferred to Leyte in late July 1944, and by late December 1944 was nearly completely annihilated during the course of the Battle of Leyte. The remainder of the division were assigned to the 41st Army and suffered heavy losses during the Battle of Manila in January 1945. It fought on until the official surrender of Japan. It is partly famous for one of its officers, Hiroo Onada, a second lieutenant of the Division, who did not surrender until 10 March 1974.","LocalizedString":"The 8th Infantry Division of the Imperial Japanese Army, formed in 1898, was nicknamed Cedar Division (杉兵団, Sugi-heidan). During WWII it served as part of the Kwantung Army in Manchuria until it was transferred to the Philippines in 1944. There, it took part in the intense combat against the US invasion. The 5th Infantry Regiment of 8th Division was transferred to Leyte in late July 1944, and by late December 1944 was nearly completely annihilated during the course of the Battle of Leyte. The remainder of the division were assigned to the 41st Army and suffered heavy losses during the Battle of Manila in January 1945. It fought on until the official surrender of Japan. It is partly famous for one of its officers, Hiroo Onada, a second lieutenant of the Division, who did not surrender until 10 March 1974."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::BloodAndIron","EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Trigger","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnBeforeStartOfTurn"],"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Veteran"],"hasBlitz":true,"hasShock":true,"spawnCardName":"card_unit_cedar_division_vet","Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Japan/Winter_2024/t_gifu_regiment_nf.t_gifu_regiment_nf","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Volmi Games","history